  "goodToKnow": "Der Leutnant is a lieutenant, the lowest officer rank in the Bundeswehr, followed by Oberleutnant and Hauptmann (captain). The word came from French lieutenant (one who holds the place of a superior), adapted to German spelling and pronounced LOYT-nant. Since 2001, women have been allowed to serve in all branches of the Bundeswehr, so Leutnant is used for both. The plural is die Leutnants."
